IMPORT prelude

-- Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016 (Singapore) -- the Authority's board: size, disqualification, quorum
-- and voting (ss 10, 12, 19, 21, 31, 33); secrecy and immunity (ss 44, 45); Part 7 media competition and control: prohibited
-- agreements, abuse of dominance and exemption (ss 62-64), the 30% controller and associate thresholds (ss 59, 60B), approval
-- of control of a regulated person (s 65), written orders and financial penalties (s 66), reconsideration and appeal (ss 67A,
-- 68); and the offences, penalties and composition (ss 9, 44, 65(8), 66(8), 74-77).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IMDAA2016.txt, labelled
-- "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 2/10/2026", with amendments to Act 13 of 2026 (wef 2 October 2026) shown.
-- Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement at the top is out of step from s 71 on (the body's s 74 is
-- "Offences relating to enforcement", which the arrangement lists as s 73).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content.
-- Not encoded: the Authority's functions and powers (ss 5-8), privatisation, meetings procedure beyond quorum and voting,
-- committees and delegation, finance, codes of practice and directions (ss 61, 61A, 65A-65C), dispute resolution (s 67),
-- separation orders (s 69A), entry and search (ss 70-72), legal privilege (s 73), liability of officers (ss 78, 79), interest
-- (s 79A), and Parts 9 and 10 (transfer, repeal, savings). The disregarded interests in ss 59(4) and 60A(3) (bare trustees,
-- lenders, underwriters, proxies, liquidators) are not modelled: the percentages given are taken to be the ones that count.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016 -- board, media control and offences`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` GREATER THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `10, 19 -- size of the Authority and term of office`

-- s 10(1): "The Authority consists of at least 6 and not more than 20 members."
-- s 19(1): "The term of appointment of a member must not exceed 3 years." (2) A member may be re-appointed.
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is lawfully constituted in size` IF
    `number of members` AT LEAST 6 AND `number of members` AT MOST 20

GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is lawful` IF `term in years` AT MOST 3

§§ `12(2), 21(1)(g) -- disqualification and vacation of office`

-- s 12(2): disqualified are (a) "a Judge or judicial officer"; (b) "an undischarged bankrupt"; (c) "an individual who has been
-- sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and has not received a free pardon"; (d) a disqualified company or
-- VCC director, during the disqualification; (e) an individual who lacks capacity under the Mental Capacity Act 2008, or under
-- an order under s 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008.
GIVEN `is a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER,
      `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a disqualified director` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is disqualified from membership` IF
        `is a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `is a disqualified director`
    OR  `lacks capacity`

-- s 21(1)(g): a member ceases to hold office if he or she "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Authority (without the
-- approval of the Authority)".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `absence approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member vacates office for absence` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `absence approved by the Authority`)

§§ `31, 33 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 31(1): "The quorum for a meeting of the Authority is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the number of members;
-- (b) 3 members." (2) No business may be transacted without a quorum.
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` AT LEAST (`the larger of` (`number of members` DIVIDED BY 3) 3)

-- s 33(2): the person presiding has, "in the case of an equality of votes at the meeting, a casting vote". (3) A decision is
-- adopted if agreed by all present without dissent "or if a majority of the votes cast on it are in favour of it". (4) A member
-- present "is presumed to have agreed to, and to have cast a vote in favour of" a decision unless he or she "expressly dissents
-- from or votes against" it. So every member present who does not expressly vote against counts as a vote in favour.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `members expressly voting against` IS A NUMBER, `casting vote is in favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is adopted` IF
    `members present` MINUS `members expressly voting against` GREATER THAN `members expressly voting against`
    OR (`members present` MINUS `members expressly voting against` EQUALS `members expressly voting against` AND `casting vote is in favour`)

§§ `44, 45 -- secrecy and protection from personal liability`

-- s 44(1): the Chief Executive, a member, employee, delegate or committee member who has information in that capacity "must not
-- disclose that information to any person except" (a) in performing the Authority's functions; (b) with the Authority's prior
-- authorisation; (c) in disclosing an interest as this Act requires; (d) "as required or allowed by this Act or any other Act";
-- (e) "as required by an order of court". (2) $2,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `in performing the Authority's functions`
    `with the Authority's prior authorisation`
    `in declaring an interest`
    `as required or allowed by an Act`
    `under a court order`
    `to a journalist`
    `to a friend over dinner`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure breaches secrecy` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `to a journalist` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to a friend over dinner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 45: no liability for anything done or omitted "in good faith and with reasonable care" in performing a function or exercising
-- a power of the Authority. Both conditions are required.
GIVEN `acting in the Authority's functions or powers` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from personal liability` IF
    `acting in the Authority's functions or powers` AND `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care`

§§ `62-64 -- prohibited agreements and abuse of dominance`

-- s 62(2): a regulated person must not engage in any agreement, decision or concerted practice "(a) that is of a nature
-- specified by the Authority in a code of practice; and (b) that has, as its object or effect, the prevention, restriction or
-- distortion of competition" in a market connected to media services in Singapore. (3) A prohibited provision is void to the
-- extent it infringes. s 64(1): the Authority may exempt any person, agreement, decision, concerted practice or conduct.
GIVEN `by a regulated person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `of a nature specified in a code of practice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `object or effect is to restrict competition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempted under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is prohibited` IF
    `by a regulated person` AND `of a nature specified in a code of practice` AND `object or effect is to restrict competition`
    AND (NOT `exempted under section 64`)

-- s 63(1): conduct of regulated persons that "amounts to an abuse of dominant position" in a media market conducted under a
-- broadcasting licence or newspaper permit, and "may, as a result, affect the media industry in Singapore", is prohibited.
-- (2) Dominance is "in the opinion of the Authority" an ability "to act without significant competitive restraint".
GIVEN `the Authority considers the regulated person dominant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the conduct is an abuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it may affect the media industry in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempted under section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct abuses a dominant position` IF
    `the Authority considers the regulated person dominant` AND `the conduct is an abuse` AND `it may affect the media industry in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `exempted under section 64`)

§§ `59, 60B, 65 -- control of a regulated person`

-- s 59(1): a "30% controller" is a person who, alone or with associates, "(a) holds 30% or more of the total equity interests"
-- or "(b) is in a position to control 30% or more of the voting power".
-- s 60B(g), (h): a corporation is an associate of a person who, alone or with associates, controls "not less than 12% of the
-- voting power" in it.
-- s 65(1)-(3): without "the prior written approval of the Authority" a person must not become a 30% controller, "acquire any
-- business of a regulated person that is conducted pursuant to a broadcasting licence or newspaper permit, or any part of any such
-- business, as a going concern", or "obtain effective control". (5) No approval is needed where the thing occurs "by virtue only
-- of any transaction prescribed". (6) In that case the regulated person (or its trustee-manager or trustee) must give written
-- notice to the Authority "within 7 days after first becoming aware of the event".
DECLARE Acquisition HAS
    `equity interest percent with associates` IS A NUMBER
    `voting power percent with associates` IS A NUMBER
    `acquires a licensed business as a going concern` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtains effective control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Authority's prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occurs only by a prescribed transaction` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `voting power percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation is an associate by voting control` IF `voting power percent` AT LEAST 12

GIVEN `the deal` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acquirer becomes a 30% controller` IF
    `the deal`'s `equity interest percent with associates` AT LEAST 30
    OR `the deal`'s `voting power percent with associates` AT LEAST 30

GIVEN `the deal` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deal is a controlled event` IF
    `the acquirer becomes a 30% controller` `the deal`
    OR `the deal`'s `acquires a licensed business as a going concern`
    OR `the deal`'s `obtains effective control`

GIVEN `the deal` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deal contravenes section 65` IF
    `the deal is a controlled event` `the deal`
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `has the Authority's prior written approval`)
    AND (NOT `the deal`'s `occurs only by a prescribed transaction`)

GIVEN `the deal` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulated person must notify the Authority within 7 days` IF
    `the deal is a controlled event` `the deal` AND `the deal`'s `occurs only by a prescribed transaction`

-- s 65(8): a trustee-manager of a regulated business trust, or trustee of a regulated trust, which contravenes s 65(6) commits
-- an offence, fine up to $10,000. (9) Not where "the regulated person is the trustee-manager or trustee". s 65(8) names no
-- offence for a regulated person that is not a trustee-manager or trustee.
GIVEN `is a trustee-manager or trustee of the regulated person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the regulated person is itself the trustee-manager or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days after becoming aware when notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustee commits the section 65(8) offence` IF
    `is a trustee-manager or trustee of the regulated person`
    AND (NOT `the regulated person is itself the trustee-manager or trustee`)
    AND `days after becoming aware when notice was given` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `66 -- written orders and financial penalties`

-- s 66(3): for an infringement, a financial penalty "not exceeding the higher of" (a) "10% of the annual turnover of that part of
-- the business ... in respect of which the infringement occurred, as ascertained from the latest audited accounts"; (b)
-- "$1 million". (4) Notice of intention and time for written representations first, unless not practicable or desirable.
GIVEN `annual turnover of the infringing business` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`annual turnover of the infringing business` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100) 1000000

-- s 66(4): notice of intention and a time for written representations are required "unless the Authority considers that it is
-- not practicable or desirable to do so".
GIVEN `gave notice and time for representations` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice requirement is met` IF
    `gave notice and time for representations` OR `the Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable`

§§ `67A, 68 -- reconsideration and appeal`

-- s 67A(2): a reconsideration request "must be filed within 14 days of the receipt of the decision". s 68(3)(d): an appeal to the
-- Minister must be made "within 14 days after the appellant is notified ... or such longer period as the Minister may allow".
-- (The encoding treats day 14 as in time.)
GIVEN `days after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reconsideration request is in time` IF `days after receipt` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `days after notification` IS A NUMBER, `longer period allowed by the Minister in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after notification` AT MOST (`the larger of` 14 `longer period allowed by the Minister in days`)

-- s 67A(3): a person must not make both a reconsideration request and an appeal on the same decision; (4) if both are made, "the
-- appeal to the Minister is deemed to be withdrawn". (5) The appeal is also deemed withdrawn where ANY OTHER person has made a
-- reconsideration request on the same decision.
GIVEN `the appellant also asked for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN, `another person asked for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is deemed withdrawn` IF
    `the appellant also asked for reconsideration` OR `another person asked for reconsideration`

-- s 67A(7), 68(6), (8): the decision "must be complied with" until the reconsideration or appeal is determined; s 68(6) allows
-- the Minister to direct otherwise in a particular case. s 68(7): "the decision of the Minister is final". (Not encoded as a rule.)

§§ `9, 44, 65(8), 66(8), 74-77 -- offences, penalties and composition`

-- s 9(2): using the Authority's symbol without permission, or a deceptive resemblance: $5,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 44(2): breach of secrecy: $2,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 65(8): trustee-manager or trustee failing to notify: $10,000 (no imprisonment).
-- s 66(8): failing "without reasonable excuse" to comply with a written order: $100,000 or 3 years or both.
-- s 74(2): failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an identity, notice, explanation or production requirement: $10,000
-- or 12 months or both. s 75(3): false or misleading information known to be so, or destroying required documents: the same.
-- s 76(2): obstructing or hindering the Authority: the same.
-- s 77(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine" and (b) "$2,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Authority's symbol`
    `breaching secrecy`
    `a trustee failing to notify a prescribed control event`
    `failing to comply with a written order`
    `failing to comply with an enforcement requirement`
    `giving false or misleading information`
    `obstructing the Authority`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breaching secrecy` THEN 2000
    WHEN `a trustee failing to notify a prescribed control event` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to comply with a written order` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `a trustee failing to notify a prescribed control event` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to comply with a written order` THEN 36
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

-- s 75(1): a person must not make a statement or provide information or a document "that the person knows to be false or
-- misleading in any material particular".
GIVEN `the statement is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person knew it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false statement offence is made out` IF
    `the statement is false or misleading` AND `in a material particular` AND `the person knew it`
